            <h3>Major Market Events Impact</h3>
            <table>
                <tr>
                    <th>Event</th>
                    <th>Peak Price</th>
                    <th>Trough Price</th>
                    <th>Drawdown</th>
                </tr>'''

for event, data in event_drawdowns.items():
    html_content += f'''
                <tr>
                    <td>{event}</td>
                    <td>${data['peak']:.2f}</td>
                    <td>${data['trough']:.2f}</td>
                    <td style="color: #e53e3e; font-weight: 600;">{data['drawdown']:.1f}%</td>
                </tr>'''

html_content += f'''
            </table>

            <div class="disclaimer">
                <strong>Note on Data:</strong> Early 1972 prices (~$1.22) are adjusted for splits and dividends per the source dataset documentation. This reflects retroactive adjustment from nominal prices, not actual trading prices at that time.
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Volatility & Risk Section -->
        <div class="section" id="volatility-risk">
            <h2>Volatility & Risk Assessment</h2>
            <p>American Express exhibits typical characteristics of a financial sector stock with elevated volatility during market stress periods. The maximum drawdown of <strong>{max_drawdown:.1f}%</strong> occurred on <strong>{max_drawdown_date.strftime('%Y-%m-%d')}</strong>, reflecting significant downside risk during major market dislocations.</p>

            <div class="chart-container">
                <h3>Historical Drawdown Analysis</h3>
                <img src="data:image/png;base64,{drawdown_chart_base64}" alt="AXP Drawdown Chart">
            </div>

            <h3>Risk Metrics Summary</h3>
            <table>
                <tr>
                    <th>Metric</th>
                    <th>Value</th>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Maximum Drawdown</td>
                    <td>{max_drawdown:.1f}%</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Annualized Volatility (Full Period)</td>
                    <td>{annualized_vol:.1f}%</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Daily Volatility (Std Dev)</td>
                    <td>{daily_vol * 100:.2f}%</td>
                </tr>
            </table>

            <div class="chart-container">
                <h3>Annual Returns Distribution</h3>
                <img src="data:image/png;base64,{annual_returns_base64}" alt="AXP Annual Returns">
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Volume Analysis Section -->
        <div class="section" id="volume-analysis">
            <h2>Trading Volume Analysis</h2>
            <p>Trading volume analysis reveals significant structural changes in AXP's liquidity profile over the decades. Early data (1972) shows zero volume, with reliable volume records beginning in later years.</p>
'''

if volume_by_decade:
    html_content += '''
            <h3>Volume Statistics by Decade</h3>
            <table>
                <tr>
                    <th>Decade</th>
                    <th>Average Volume</th>
                    <th>Median Volume</th>
                    <th>Peak Volume</th>
                </tr>'''
    for decade, data in volume_by_decade.items():
        html_content += f'''
                <tr>
                    <td>{decade}</td>
                    <td>{data['avg_volume']:,.0f}</td>
                    <td>{data['median_volume']:,.0f}</td>
                    <td>{data['max_volume']:,.0f}</td>
                </tr>'''
    html_content += '''
            </table>'''

html_content += f'''
            <div class="chart-container">
                <h3>Volume Trend (50-day Moving Average)</h3>
                <img src="data:image/png;base64,{volume_chart_base64}" alt="AXP Volume Chart">
            </div>

            <p><strong>Note:</strong> Early 1970s data shows Volume = 0 due to data unavailability for that period, as documented in the source dataset.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Dividends & Splits Section -->
        <div class="section" id="dividends-splits">
            <h2>Dividend History & Stock Splits</h2>
            <p>American Express has maintained a consistent dividend policy, returning value to shareholders through regular cash distributions. Total dividends paid per share over the analysis period: <strong>${total_dividends:.2f}</strong>.</p>

            <div class="chart-container">
                <h3>Annual Dividend Per Share</h3>
                <img src="data:image/png;base64,{dividend_chart_base64}" alt="AXP Dividends">
            </div>
'''

if len(split_events) > 0:
    html_content += '''
            <h3>Stock Split Events</h3>
            <table>
                <tr>
                    <th>Date</th>
                    <th>Split Ratio</th>
                </tr>'''
    for _, row in split_events.iterrows():
        html_content += f'''
                <tr>
                    <td>{row['Date'].strftime('%Y-%m-%d')}</td>
                    <td>{row['Stock Splits']:.1f}-for-1</td>
                </tr>'''
    html_content += '''
            </table>'''
else:
    html_content += '''
            <p><em>Note: Prices are already adjusted for splits and dividends per the source dataset documentation. No split events appear in the raw data with non-zero values.</em></p>'''

html_content += f'''
            <h3>Dividend Yield Analysis</h3>
            <p>The dividend yield has evolved over time as the stock price appreciated. Based on current trailing dividends and the latest price of ${last_price:.2f}, the indicated dividend yield is approximately <strong>${df[df['Date'] >= '2025-01-01']['Dividends'].sum():.2f}</strong> annually (full-year estimate).</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Decade Comparison Section -->
        <div class="section" id="decade-comparison">
            <h2>Decade-by-Decade Performance Comparison</h2>
            <p>Comparing performance across decades reveals varying market conditions and return profiles. The 1980s and 2010s were particularly strong, while the 2000s faced significant headwinds from the dot-com bust and financial crisis.</p>

            <div class="chart-container">
                <h3>Total Return by Decade</h3>
                <img src="data:image/png;base64,{decade_chart_base64}" alt="AXP Decade Returns">
            </div>

            <div class="chart-container">
                <h3>Annualized Volatility by Decade</h3>
                <img src="data:image/png;base64,{vol_chart_base64}" alt="AXP Decade Volatility">
            </div>

            <h3>Decade Performance Metrics</h3>
            <table>
                <tr>
                    <th>Decade</th>
                    <th>Starting Price</th>
                    <th>Ending Price</th>
                    <th>Total Return</th>
                    <th>CAGR</th>
                    <th>Volatility</th>
                    <th>Dividends</th>
                </tr>'''

for decade, stats in decades.items():
    if stats:
        html_content += f'''
                <tr>
                    <td>{decade}</td>
                    <td>${stats['start_price']:.2f}</td>
                    <td>${stats['end_price']:.2f}</td>
                    <td style="color: {'#38a169' if stats['return'] >= 0 else '#e53e3e'}; font-weight: 600;">{stats['return']:+.1f}%</td>
                    <td>{stats['cagr']:+.1f}%</td>
                    <td>{stats['volatility']:.1f}%</td>
                    <td>${stats['dividends']:.2f}</td>
                </tr>'''

html_content += '''
            </table>

            <h3>Key Observations</h3>
            <ul style="margin: 15px 0 15px 30px;">
                <li><strong>Best Decade:</strong> '''

# Find best and worst decades
best_decade = max(decades.items(), key=lambda x: x[1]['return'] if x[1] else -999)
worst_decade = min(decades.items(), key=lambda x: x[1]['return'] if x[1] else 999)

html_content += f'''{best_decade[0]} ({best_decade[1]['return']:+.1f}% total return)</li>
                <li><strong>Worst Decade:</strong> {worst_decade[0]} ({worst_decade[1]['return']:+.1f}% total return)</li>
                <li><strong>Most Volatile:</strong> {max(decades.items(), key=lambda x: x[1]['volatility'] if x[1] else 0)[0]} ({max(decades.items(), key=lambda x: x[1]['volatility'] if x[1] else 0)[1]['volatility']:.1f}% annualized)</li>
                <li><strong>Least Volatile:</strong> {min(decades.items(), key=lambda x: x[1]['volatility'] if x[1] else 999)[0]} ({min(decades.items(), key=lambda x: x[1]['volatility'] if x[1] else 999)[1]['volatility']:.1f}% annualized)</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="footer">
            <p><strong>Report Generated:</strong> ''' + datetime.now().strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S') + '''</p>
            <p>Data Source: American Express (AXP) Stock Data (1972–2026) | Analysis Period: June 1972 – March 2026</p>
            <p style="margin-top: 15px; font-size: 0.8em;">This report is for informational purposes only and does not constitute investment advice. Past performance does not guarantee future results.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</html>'''

# Write report
with open('/app/output/final_report.html', 'w') as f:
    f.write(html_content)

print("Report generated successfully: /app/output/final_report.html")
print(f"\nReport Statistics:")
print(f"  - Cumulative Return: {cumulative_return:,.0f}%")
print(f"  - CAGR: {cagr:.2f}%")
print(f"  - Max Drawdown: {max_drawdown:.1f}%")
print(f"  - Annualized Volatility: {annualized_vol:.1f}%")
print(f"  - Total Dividends: ${total_dividends:.2f}")
print(f"  - Data Points: {len(df):,}")

